Error catalog: message, meaning, action

Errors name the cause first. Find the exact bytes below, then fix
the named cause. Lint text is path plus line shaped. Runtime why
carries the first failure. The CLI lives at cmd/main.c. Code wins
over prose. If you get the category wrong you will fix the wrong
layer: lint means the file shape is bad and nothing ran, skip means
the run was not testable here, fail means the system was tested and
found wrong, and usage error means the command line never started
work.

Lint errors: categories

Lint checks shape, not behavior. It never needs root. A lint failure
means no mesh ran, so do not read logs or wipe state: open the YAML
reference at the named section, fix the named key, and rerun the
linter. For the full rule table do not copy from here; docs/yaml is
the authority with per-key scope, ranges, and its own code map. Lint
prints path plus line plus message. Unknown keys fail through the
unknown-key path. Validate with make suite-lint or bin/rsuite lint.
List success does not imply lint success.

Where to look per category:

Each entry below names a symptom, what it means, and the
fix. Open docs/yaml at the named section for the full rule.

Top keys: exactly 11 allowed, unknown fails - file has a
key outside the schema. Fix: remove or rename the key; see
Top-level keys in docs/yaml.

Name, version, sut, nodes, domain, topic: type plus range
plus SUT scope - a scalar has the wrong type, range, or
SUT. Fix: fix the named scalar; see docs/yaml.

Spawn variant, node, offset: plain, anchor, skew shapes
plus weld limits - spawn mapping breaks the variant rules.
Fix: fix variant, node, or offset; see docs/yaml.

ros_peers list: weld-only, node plus distro, non-empty max
100 - peer list breaks weld-only or entry rules. Fix: fix
the peer entries; see docs/yaml.

timeout_s file and phase plus hold_s: 1..3600 and 0..3600,
hold needs until and must not exceed phase timeout - a
timeout is out of range or hold is misplaced. Fix: fix the
timeout or hold; see Limits in docs/yaml.

phases list: non-empty, unique names, exactly one of until
or sustain - phase list is empty, doubled, or missing its
check. Fix: fix the phase list; see docs/yaml.

steps: exactly one verb per map, only drop, heal, kill,
restart, move, submit, stop, pub exist; node ints are
0..nodes-1; image, flags, topic shapes checked - a step
names a bad verb, node, or string shape. Fix: fix the step;
see docs/yaml.

conditions: exactly one of peers, marker, present, absent,
observed, assigned, mesh_count; arity and SUT scope differ
per condition - a condition names the wrong key or scope.
Fix: fix the condition; see docs/yaml plus the oracle
table.

needs verbs: unknown fails lint; single submit, stop or
workload read with no earlier submit fails, second submit
fails - a needs verb is unknown or the submit order is
wrong. Fix: fix needs or submit order; see Needs table and
Limits.

Action for any lint line: open docs/yaml at the named section, fix
the named key, rerun bin/rsuite lint.

Runtime skips: not failures

Skip means not testable here. CI reads it as not applicable. A skip
needs setup, not forensics: giving it the missing binary, daemon, or
privilege makes it run. No wipe issue, exit 0 at rsuite level per
tally. If you treat a skip as a pass of the system, you will claim
coverage that never ran.

Each entry below names a symptom, its cause, and the fix.

skip unmet need, with stdout suite: skip plus unmet need -
file needs a driver ability this SUT build lacks. Fix: run
a file whose needs match, or add the ability; lint would
have failed unknown verbs first.

skip no concord binary, with stdout suite: skip plus no
bin - concord SUT file but binary not executable at
./bin/concord or the configured concord path. Fix: build
the binary, then rerun; concord-unaffected files still run;
check shape mirrors the check skips.

skip no weld binary, same bytes on the weld path, null
means default - weld binary missing. Fix: build it or point
the suite options weld path at it.

skip no docker, with stdout suite: skip plus no docker -
weld file but docker info answers nonzero, missing, or hung
past its bound. Fix: start the docker daemon, then rerun;
concord files are unaffected and only the weld branch checks
docker.

skip with errno text, with stdout suite: skip plus errno
text - TUN open failed after unwind with errno kept; the sim
layer also prints skip with errno on host tun open, and
check TUN tests print tun_netns: skip and tun_drop: skip.
Fix: confirm with bin/rsuite doctor, rerun with root for
netns plus TUN; see the troubleshoot file for the TUN
path.

Runtime fails

Fail means tested and wrong, or setup broke. Failed runs call
forensics before wipe, so read the saved copies, not the wiped
statedir. If you rerun before reading forensics you destroy the only
evidence.

Each entry below names a symptom, its cause, and the fix.
Failed runs call forensics before wipe, so read the saved
copies, not the wiped statedir.

run acquire failed, with sim counter read, corrupt, or
exhausted text on stderr - lock, I/O, corrupt counter, or
full at 154. Fix: inspect
/var/tmp/resonance-runs.counter, wipe it to reset monotonic
ids after runs end.

bad run id with a number - id below 0 or above 154 would
wrap the octet or alias tun names. Fix: pass 0..154 only; 0
self-acquires.

setup failed - netns, nodes, or addrs step failed; partial
setup already unwound. Fix: read prior stdout, check
doctor, clean stale netns and cgroups, rerun.

statedir too long - per-run statedir did not fit the 128
byte dir cap. Fix: shorten statedir; this needs a code
change, not a flag.

spawn failed plus suite: fail plus spawn - spawn returned
false after teardown with no forensics. Fix: check binary
present plus exec ok, check statedir writable and
dev-capable, read logs.

spawn node plus number failed plus suite: fail spawn; same
for one weld node; ros peer plus index failed plus suite:
fail ros peer - weld spawn or ROS peer start returned
false. Fix: check weld binary, domain, docker, topic
charset.

phase name plus step reason, plus suite: fail plus phase
plus step - a do step failed on entry, for example a bad
step. Fix: fix the named step verb or target.

phase name plus no child alive - liveness check found none
during until or sustain. Fix: look for early exit or kill,
read per-node logs and forensics tails.

phase name plus file timeout - wall clock passed file
timeout_s. Fix: raise timeout_s within 1..3600 or split the
file; check SUT slowness in docs/speed.

phase name plus until timeout on description - phase timeout
passed before until latched plus held. Fix: check mesh
first, then fault scope, then timeout values.

phase name plus sustain violated on description - sustain
broke, or broke on exact expiry poll; this is the
hold-that-must-never-break shape. Fix: read which target
showed the banned text or lost the hold, narrow the fault.

phase name plus query reason - query layer errored. Fix:
read the query text, check statedir and query paths.

no log path on stderr - forensics tail found no log file.
Fix: check statedir and SUT split; weld versus concord
names differ.

separator line plus log path then bytes then blank - tail
of one node log. Fix: read it for peers markers and error
lines.

suite: forensics at plus dir - aside dir holding copies
past wipe, named statedir-fail with suite plus seconds.
Fix: open that dir, not the wiped statedir.

child killed on parent why when child did not exit - rsuite
child killed by signal. Fix: check signal source, rerun
with fewer jobs or serial.

(no log) in the failures list when per-file log missing or
empty - log never opened or zero bytes; bytes still phase
scanned. Fix: check log dir writable, disk space, name
clash cap.

Usage errors: exit 2

Bad CLI use prints the cause plus full usage and returns exit 2
before any child starts. Nothing ran, so do not read suite logs: fix
the command line. If you mistake exit 2 for a suite failure you will
debug the YAML when the flag order is the bug.

rsuite: needs a subcommand plus usage. Action: pass lint, run, list,
doctor, or --help.

rsuite: unknown subcommand plus name plus usage. Action: fix the
verb.

lint needs at least one file; list needs at least one file; run
needs at least one file. Action: pass a YAML path.

run needs a value after --jobs. Bad --jobs value plus text plus
usage means the parser rejects empty, leading space, non-numeric
tail, or value below 1. Action: pass --jobs N or --jobs=N with N
1..64.

rsuite: --jobs value clamped to 64. Meaning: above the max jobs cap
warns and caps. Action: none; the run proceeds at 64.

run needs a value after --log-dir. run needs a non-empty --log-dir.
Meaning: the flag needs a non-empty dir value in both spellings.
Action: pass --log-dir D or --log-dir=D.

rsuite: unknown flag plus name plus usage. Action: move a valid flag
before files or fix spelling.

--tap and --json conflict. Meaning: the two flags conflict. Action:
pass at most one.

rsuite: flag plus name after files; flags precede files plus usage.
Meaning: trailing flags are usage errors; run flags precede files.
Action: reorder flags before YAML paths.

doctor takes no arguments. Action: run bin/rsuite doctor bare.

rsuite: no log dir plus dir plus errno and rsuite: no log dir plus
errno on stderr. Meaning: custom dir not makable or temp dir failed;
the run continues with null log. Action: fix perms or path, or pass
--log-dir.

rsuite: no mem. rsuite: no signal watch. Meaning: parent alloc or
signal setup failed. Action: retry on a healthy host.

Doctor: OK, MISSING, ERROR

Doctor reports setup, it does not fail for missing tools. Each line
is OK, MISSING, or ERROR: positive status prints OK, zero prints
MISSING plus hint, negative prints ERROR plus hint. Doctor exits 0
with the report even when lines say MISSING, and 1 only on probe
error, since missing deps inform rather than fail. If you gate
scripts on the words instead of the exit, you will fail healthy
hosts that simply lack an optional daemon.

Lines in order: euid root OK when root else MISSING (not root);
/dev/net/tun OK on read plus write else MISSING (no tun access);
netns list; create needs root via shell ip netns list, MISSING (ip
missing) or ERROR on fork or wait failure; bin/concord sibling of
rsuite OK on exec else MISSING (not built); bin/weld same; docker
daemon via shell docker info MISSING (daemon down) or ERROR on probe
failure; run lock read plus write on /var/tmp/resonance-runs.lock
else MISSING (missing or denied); run counter same on
/var/tmp/resonance-runs.counter; lock dir /var/tmp write plus exec
else MISSING (not writable). Lock and counter paths mirror the sim
allocator paths.

Code map

Lint format and unknown-key helpers; extra-key check; top key range
and per-key scalar checks; spawn variant shapes; ROS peer list
checks; timeout and hold checks; phase list checks; step verb checks
with image, flags, topic, float, and durability helpers; condition
checks with oracle table in the header; needs table and submit order
checks. Skip branches: unmet need, concord binary, weld binary,
docker probe, errno path; TUN open and check skip prints. Fail
branches: acquire, run id, setup, statedir length, spawn paths,
phase step and liveness and timeout and sustain and query paths,
forensics tail and aside dir, child signal, missing log list. Usage
exit path and global help; per-command missing-file, jobs, log-dir,
flag, conflict, order, and doctor-arity errors; log dir and alloc
failures. Doctor line printer, shell probe helper, sibling resolver,
and ordered probe list with lock and counter paths.
